        "content": "Jute, the 'Golden Fiber', is the second most crucial natural bast fiber after cotton. Cultivated extensively in West Bengal, Bihar, and Assam, it is an eco-friendly, biodegradable industrial packaging fiber.\n\n### Botanical Comparison: Tossa vs White Jute\n- **Tossa Jute (*Corchorus olitorius* L.):** Deep yellowish-brown to golden silky fiber, higher tensile strength, softer texture, cultivated on well-drained uplands (intolerant of waterlogging in early stages); cylindrical 5-valved pods; varieties: JRO 524 (Navin), JRO 204.\n- **White Jute (*Corchorus capsularis* L.):** Whitish, coarser, weaker fiber, highly tolerant of prolonged waterlogging and flooding (deep-water tracts); globular rounded capsules; bitter leaves (due to glucoside *corchorin*); varieties: JRC 321, JRC 212.\n\n### Biochemistry of Water Retting\nRetting is a controlled biological and biochemical process wherein anaerobic and aerobic pectinolytic microorganisms degrade the pectic mucilage, gums, and hemicellulose binding bast fiber bundles to the inner woody stem (stick/hurd), releasing clean intact fiber strands.\n- **Submersion Protocol:** Harvested stems are bundled, defoliated, and steeped in clean, slow-flowing water ($32\\text{\u2013}34^\\circ\\text{C}$ optimal). Bundles are weighed down using concrete blocks or aquatic weeds (never mud, banana stems, or iron weights, which turn fibers dark grey or pitch black through iron-tannin reactions, a defect known as 'Shyamla color').\n- **Microbial Catalysts:** Pectinolytic enzymes (pectin lyase, polygalacturonase) secreted by *Clostridium*, *Bacillus*, and *Macrophomina* digest pectins within 12\u201318 days.\n- **CRIJAF Sona Formulation:** ICAR-CRIJAF developed an advanced bacterial microbial consortium (CRIJAF Sona) that shortens retting duration by 6\u20137 days, eliminates foul odor, and upgrades fiber quality by 2\u20133 grades.\n\n### Ribbon Retting Technology\nMechanically peeling the green bark (ribbon) from harvested green stalks using a mechanical decorticator and retting only the ribbons in small polythene-lined micro-ponds drastically slashes water requirements (by 60\u201370%), accelerates retting to 7\u20138 days, and completely avoids fiber handling of heavy woody sticks.",
